Vikram and Betal: The Lost Horse (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100137

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a man whose horse went missing,” said Betal. “He searched everywhere but could not find it.”

He went to the king for help.

The king called a wise man to solve the problem.

The wise man said, “Bring all the villagers here.”

When everyone gathered, he said, “The thief among you has touched the horse. His hands will smell different.”

The villagers became nervous.

The wise man then walked around and smelled their hands.

He suddenly stopped near one man and said, “You are the thief!”

The man became scared and confessed.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, how did the wise man know?”

Vikram replied, “Because the guilty man was afraid and behaved differently.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Fear reveals the truth.
